   196	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   197	    """Extrapolate the moving sprite into the next standalone panel, transferring blocked motion to the grey bar.
   198	
   199	    Input structure:
   200	    - The grid is a horizontal sequence of equal-width framed panels that share vertical border columns.
   201	    - Every panel has the same fill color, the same grey horizontal obstacle bar, and the same inner sprite.
   202	    - The sprite keeps the same local columns and its top row changes by a constant amount from panel to panel.
   203	
   204	    Rule:
   205	    - Parse the shared-border frame sequence and infer the per-panel vertical displacement from successive sprite positions.
   206	    - Convert that displacement to the standalone next frame by scaling from shared-border stride to full panel width.
   207	    - Starting from the last observed panel, move the sprite one cell at a time in that vertical direction; if the next step would overlap the grey bar, stop the sprite.
   208	    - Transfer every unspent step to the grey bar, moving the bar in the same direction until the requested steps are exhausted or the bar hits the inner frame border.
   209	
   210	    Key insight:
   211	    - This is not pure extrapolation: the last frame first predicts a naive next sprite position, but any blocked remainder becomes a second motion applied to the obstacle itself.
